Lexifina's own contributions in this repository (the arrangement of the history, the file layout, the commit messages
and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The legal text is from the Barbados Law Courts site of the Barbados Judicial System (https://www.barbadoslawcourts.gov.bb):
the Statutes of Barbados and the Subsidiary Legislation of Barbados (consolidated by the Law Revision Office,
https://www.barbadoslawcourts.gov.bb/laws/consolidated-laws), and the annual Acts and statutory instruments
(https://www.barbadoslawcourts.gov.bb/laws/annuals), retrieved from 3 November 2026 on. The site states no licence;
its footer reads "Copyright Barbados Judicial System. All Rights Reserved." and its Terms & Conditions link leads
nowhere. Its robots.txt asks for a 10-second crawl delay, which was kept, and does not restrict these files. The
legal text is reproduced for reference with attribution to the publisher, and remains subject to whatever rights the
Government of Barbados holds in it; this repository claims none.

The text is the PDFs' own text layer. Where that layer was made by the publisher from page scans it is taken as
served, with its recognition errors, and each such commit says so in its Text-source trailer. No OCR was run for this
repository.

Changes made by Lexifina: running heads and page numbers were removed, marginal notes were set aside where the PDF
sets them in a smaller type, and each text was split into one Markdown file per section and schedule. The wording of
the law was not changed. The Government of Barbados and the Barbados Judicial System do not endorse this repository.
This repository is not legal advice and not an official publication.
